# Frontend Guardrails

## API Usage

- Use [frontend/src/api/client.ts](mdc:frontend/src/api/client.ts) for HTTP calls.
- Do not hardcode localhost API URLs; use [frontend/src/lib/http.ts](mdc:frontend/src/lib/http.ts).
- Use [frontend/src/lib/error.ts](mdc:frontend/src/lib/error.ts) for user-friendly error messages.

## UX Consistency

- Important actions (delete/role change/deactivate) should use custom confirmation modal, not `window.confirm`.
- Preserve role-specific visibility and actions across pages.
- Keep counters/KPIs in sync after mutations (optimistic update and/or refetch).

## Forms

- Trim string inputs before submit.
- Keep create vs edit flows explicit to reduce user confusion.
- Prefer modal edit for list-heavy admin pages when scroll context matters.
